; Gollum asks his riddle
;
; Script handler (op 3, in Gollum's script #R$C9F7). When Gollum is where the
; player is and the player is visible (not wearing the ring: flag bit 7 of
; the player is set) the test pass accepts and Gollum says the riddle chosen
; at the start of the game (RandomEventPtr: the message word at +2 of the
; record in #R$C7FC; the riddle of the dark or the riddle of the animal with
; four feet). It sets ReplyGiven to 1, so that the answer is looked for by
; #R$A8F6. Otherwise it returns before the test pass accepts and the script
; takes its alternative step (#R$CA10).
; .
; Hardware: none (the text goes through the message printer).
@label=GollumAsksRiddle
c$A8D2 LD A,($C4C1)  ; Gollum's location
 $A8D5 LD HL,$B6F5   ; player's location
 $A8D8 CP (HL)
 $A8D9 RET NZ        ; not together: refuse
 $A8DA LD HL,$C122
@isub=BIT FLAG_PRESENT,(HL)
 $A8DD BIT 7,(HL)    ; player invisible: refuse
 $A8DF RET Z
 $A8E0 CALL $9D44
 $A8E3 LD HL,($B6EE) ; the chosen random event
 $A8E6 INC HL        ; skip the phrase code
 $A8E7 INC HL
 $A8E8 LD E,(HL)
 $A8E9 INC HL
 $A8EA LD D,(HL)
 $A8EB PUSH DE
 $A8EC POP HL
 $A8ED CALL $A1E3    ; say the riddle
 $A8F0 LD A,$01
 $A8F2 LD ($B6F9),A  ; ReplyGiven := 1: waiting for the answer
 $A8F5 RET
